<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10000"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 3:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Topsy, <BR> <BR>Sorry I hijacked your thread, girl. There were some weird emotions going off while the cat was away. Things escalated after the dirty dog was caught. It just seemed like we all needed to come together. <BR> <BR>I think I might need to apologize for something else it did last night, but I can’t really remember things too clearly. It’s just… well, this is not my underwear! Anyone? <BR> <BR>OH MY HEAD! Ouch, take the caps lock off! <BR> <BR>I’m starting up a 12 steps thread later. <BR> <BR>What did you put in mine George? I swear to my God I “never will ever”.. ever drink a Train Wreck again… ever… <BR> <BR>…OK, maybe just a taste after the sentence comes down! <BR> <BR> <BR>Here is another reason we had to party. <BR> <BR>Dennis The Menace absolutely posted here. I am 100% convinced that we did help CatchBTK. We rattled his brain, cost him valuable time, forced him to ruminate on a boundless fantasy world that he wasn’t prepared to deal with. <BR> <BR>I would be proud to know if I&#40;as ClaireVoient, PleaseDeleteMe or FloydW&#41; was on his “little list”. Our cat calls, near misses and direct hits made him indulge in very dangerous thoughts about us. <BR> <BR>While he was picturing how he could find Claire, tie her up, teach her some respect and send her to Jesus, he should have been reading Final Affair by McAdams and Carney. <BR> <BR>Use a floppy, go to jail. <BR> <BR>I was dead serious when I said posters like Huff and Skov and George confounded and yes – mesmerized Rader. They were talking about him…a lot. He had to pay attention. He had to. <BR> <BR>Fame is a bitch. DTM bought in to his own myth and it led to his downfall. Steven Segal could learn a thing or two here. <BR> <BR>He should have been mustering all the clarity he was capable of. Instead, he was forced to obsess about his public. <BR> <BR>While he was raging inside over Steve_huff’s wicked critique of his poetry, he should have been researching how to fake his own death and disappearance. <BR> <BR>When George originally insisted that Marine Hedge and Dee Davis were his victims, Denny scheduled more time and less sleep to make sure he didn’t miss a post. <BR>He should have been studying up on exchange rates for Cruzados. <BR> <BR>As Skov scoured 68,000,100 Google results for keyword Kansas, Denny must have been wondering…   <BR> <BR>“WHO IS SKOV? G&#42;DDAMMIT! Has she seen my Park City page? Lost Dog… what the hell was I thinking? Denmark my ass! That was her glaring at me in Applebee’s after church. No…no…stop. Must sleep, 3:15… Lynn rAder roars…HE ROARS... They never will ever… SLEEP… beat me… Oh Jesus, let me sleep… North of… Ketchi… Q… Who is Q?... Quincy? Quintana? …Iq… 3:21…&#40;sighs&#41;… &#40;bump&#41; Huh? what was that?... &#40;stops breathing, ears ringing&#41;…damn dogs…what time… 3:22…&#40;tick tock tick tock&#41;… …&#40;tick tock tick&#41; … … sorry momma I could no…When you hit… the end of the rope... your muscles lose control... I&#39;m afraid… I&#39;ll mess mysel…HUH!.. 4:22…Voight…Thomas… vvvvvvvv…oi...oi...oi… Tommy… Tom… moT…Vom… VomiT… go VomiT at shh… no…oh goT him Vast…no… goT ham…no… goTham host iV… 4:40… &#40;tick tock&#41;…Oh Jesus, let me sleep…” <BR> <BR>He was here Topsail.  <BR>Posting as B•T•K? -- Maybe.  <BR>His stench ran through our threads and we ran through his head.  <BR>His posts sent us on a wild goose chase. <BR>Our posts sent him to the freezing shed at 4:40am to see if anyone was getting close. <BR> <BR>The hangover was worth it. <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
