<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10744"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 10:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bluepup, I find that really, really weird. It could always just be one of those co-inky-dinks, sure - but the spelling is is precise - R-A-D-E-R. <BR> <BR>Which is a bigger point than folks may realize. I&#39;ve seen Denny the Deadly Dog Catcher&#39;s last name misspelled in the following ways since his arrest: <BR> <BR>- Rayder <BR>- Radar <BR>- Raider <BR>- Raidar <BR> <BR>And I&#39;m not sure that&#39;s all. Point is, that&#39;s a very specific spelling. And the time of the post is interesting, too.  <BR> <BR>BTW...anyone seen the poster going by &#34;Gotcha&#34; in a while? If you are Gotcha and you&#39;re reading this, my apologies in advance.  <BR> <BR>But, in the same thread where Bluepup found that post from a &#34;Rader&#34;, there was this post by Gotcha: <BR> <BR><i>Posted on Friday, <b>January 07, 2005</b> - 9:06 pm:   	 <BR>you are way off base Crimone, BTK just turned <b>59</b> and worked at <b>Coleman</b>.</i> <BR> <BR>Only post I&#39;ve found anywhere to nail BTK&#39;s age and state <u>definitively</u> that he worked at Coleman...nearly 2 months before his arrest. I added the bolding of certain words I found significant.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
