<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10969"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 2:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There also was a one-time poster who used the name Francis Dolarhyde which was the fictional name of a serial killer from the Thomas Harris novel that was made into the 2002 movie &#39;Red Dragon&#39;. <BR>Francis Dolarhyde posted on November 23rd at 9 am: <BR>BTK, Fear nothing. Keep thy strength. <BR>I have been and shall forever remain your...Avid Fan.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
