<!--Post: 11079--><!--Time: 1110418010-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11079"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 5:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rae! <BR> <BR>Thanks for the tour of your dig site. Nice find! <BR> <BR>I remember reading this post and blowing it off. <BR>A female poetry writing accomplice? Right! <BR>Sorry Larry WhateverYourNameIs. <BR>NEXT! <BR> <BR>Fast forward. <BR> <BR>BiTtaKer? <BR>Audio-taped torture? <BR>Polaroids? <BR>Isn’t that a silver van in Rader’s driveway? Rocky? <BR> <BR>This was Bittaker’s 1979 M.O. – stalk, abduct, bind, rape and torture, strangle, document, dispose. <BR>Bittaker had an accomplice and his victims were teenaged, Rader was a confessed copycat and apparently… inspired. <BR> <BR>It seems Rader fed off of Bittaker’s “X” to the extent that he drastically reworked his own M.O. <BR> <BR>Using only confirmed BTK victims, Rader commences his ritual of emulation with Marine Hedge &#40;4/27/85&#41; and concludes with Dee Davis &#40;1/19/1991&#41;. <BR> <BR> <BR>…Yet, there is one more confirmed victim to consider and she predates any discovery of a Bittaker victim by seven months. <BR> <BR> <BR>“Magicians stop thinking too soon” <BR>-- Dai Vernon <BR> <BR>Dai Vernon was a master of close-up magic. <BR>He could simultaneously make a miracle happen in the palm of your hand, <BR>and a memory that would last a lifetime in your head. <BR>“Professor” Vernon was a brilliant conceptual and analytical thinker who inspired a renaissance in the field of conjuring.   <BR>His quote referred to the propensity of performers to rush an effect to the stage without considering the next level of amazement. <BR>He could have been referring to any profession and he would have made a great detective. <BR>I always lean on “The Professor” to defend my need to analyze things to death. <BR> <BR>Serial killers are a virus -- take it from a Southern California native. <BR> <BR>So who infected Bittaker?…  a disease called KenneTh Bianchi seems logical. <BR> <BR>c. 1978 -- In a recliner, in family room, in Park City, Kansas, a monster’s gut was smoldering. <BR>A toddler played quietly on the floor. A pregnant wife practiced a hymn while preparing comfort food. In the gut, an admiration and an idea festered. <BR>Talking heads on the evening news described gruesome discoveries: <BR>…strangled female bodies in the weeds of Los Angeles. The accompanying images were projected into a dark fantasy world. <BR> <BR> “Oh, Anna… <BR>… Drop of fear fresh Spring rain would roll down from your nakedness… <BR>... Bed of Spring moist grass, clean before the sun, enslaved with <BR>control, warm wind scenting the air, sun light sparkle tears <BR>in eyes so deep and clear… <BR> <BR>“Oh, Anna” is more than a killer’s lament, it’s an announcement. <BR> <BR>“I am changing my M.O.” <BR> <BR>“Oh, Anna” is about a body… lying in the open, washed by April rains, exposed to the elements and decaying.    <BR> <BR>Had Anna Williams not been having the time of her life on the evening of April 29, 1979, she would have been next… and she might have been a first as well. <BR> <BR>While Rader felt free to return to his earlier M.O., as was the case with Vicki Wegerle, he had a new fetish. <BR> <BR>Women of a preceding generation would be destroyed, transported and disposed of in the wide open spaces surrounding Wichita. <BR> <BR>When “Oh Anna” was released to the media, WPD announced that Anna Williams daughter was likely the intended victim. <BR> <BR>They did not publicly announce that Marine Hedge and Dee Davis were BTK victims until the BTK was nothing more than a hairy ball of dough in a red jumpsuit. <BR> <BR>Initially, Rader was motivated to communicate when others were credited with his slaughter. <BR>Investigators may have purposely planted the “William’s daughter” story or downplayed Hedge and Davis in hopes that BTK would call…and maybe he did. <BR> <BR>Or perhaps the connections were only made after the arrest. <BR> <BR>Somewhere in these threads someone must have made the same analysis of “Oh Anna”. If not here, then in the cluttered closets of AMW or the Eagle boards. I’m just too worn out to read the posts again. <BR> <BR>Before someone slams me for being a Monday morning quarterback or a time waster – allow me to paste a portion of something I posted in a thread where those very same aspersions were directed at my fellow posters: <BR> <BR>“Recent polls at CatchBTK show a decided lack of confidence in LE’s ability to get all the goods. <BR> <BR>History shows that calculating brutes &#40;think Bundy or Henry Lee&#41; get perks and bus rides and LOTS OF ATTENTION when they practice a slow reveal of their secret crimes. <BR> <BR>Rader may rot, but has BTK really been caught until all his victims see justice?” <BR> <BR>If Rader was prepared to pose Anna in a field that night, how does this reflect on similar unsolved murders or the possibility of shifting M.O.s as early as spring of 1979? <BR> <BR> <BR>Other notes on the Bittaker post: <BR> <BR>I searched for and found the Gender Geni&#40;sic&#41; through a site called TB2K! <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.bookblog.net/gender/genie.html" target=_top>http://www.bookblog.net/gender/genie.html</a> <BR> <BR>The Genie is most accurate when analyzing texts of 500 words or more. <BR> <BR>According to an analysis of my own writing, I am half man, half woman. <BR> <BR> <BR>Yours Truly, <BR> <BR>Lady&amp;theTrampDog <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
