<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11102"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 8:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The BTK Strangler demanded recognition as a successful serial murderer. Its possible Rader admired the series of murders committed by Lawrence Bittaker and Roy Norris. It seems he admired Bundy and Berkowitz. Bittaker and Norris abducted teenage girls in 1979 in Southern Californa. They raped and strangled them in a van Bittaker baptized &#39;Murder Mack&#39;. Bittaker and Norris made audio recordings of the murders to symbolize their conquest.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
