<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11109"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 9:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry to hear that Chiqui. <BR> <BR>I hope it was my androgyny and not the creepy subject matter that turned you off! <BR> <BR>I doubled checked the Gender Genie and this time it revealed that I’m a manly man who’s really in touch with his feminine side. Think of Hemingway channeling Louisa May Alcott. <BR> <BR>About that post: <BR> <BR>It doesn’t really belong in this thread. <BR> <BR>I was riffing off the potential BTK post that Rae dug up and stumbled onto a new &#40;for me&#41; interpretation of “Oh Anna”. <BR> <BR>I did skim the Poetry threads &#40;some of the best on Catch&#41; and did not see any similar conclusions. <BR> <BR>I’m going to find a more appropriate place to post this, though I have a problem with the title of the Anna Williams thread. <BR> <BR> <BR>LouisaDog <BR> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
