<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11120"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 11:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lil, <BR> <BR>I just reread my stream of consciousness rap disguised as a post. <BR> <BR> What the h…?!?! <BR> <BR>I shouldn’t have skipped lunch today. <BR>Low blood sugar can be a dangerous thing. <BR> <BR>Believe it or not, I did have a point. Here it is. <BR> <BR>From the day the “Oh Anna” poem was received until Rader’s arrest, authorities have maintained that BTK was probably waiting for Anna William’s daughter. It was taken for granted that BTK would leave the young woman’s body in the house had she… appeared. <BR> <BR>I am convinced Dennis Rader, then 34, intended to kill Anna Williams, a 63 year old woman. <BR>Furthermore, I believe he was prepared to dispose of her body in a manner similar to that of Marine Hedge &#40;1985&#41; and Dee Davis &#40;1991&#41;. <BR> <BR>The clues are in the poem: <BR> <BR>“Oh, Anna… <BR> <BR>… Drop of fear fresh Spring rain would roll down from your nakedness… <BR> <BR>... Bed of Spring moist grass, clean before the sun, enslaved with <BR>control, warm wind scenting the air, sun light sparkle tears <BR>in eyes so deep and clear… <BR> <BR>In “Oh, Anna” Rader is waxing…about a body… posed in the outdoors, washed by April rains, exposed to the elements and decaying. <BR> <BR>Six years later, nearly to the day, Marine Hedge, 58, meets an identical fate.    <BR> <BR>The poem announces a sea change in the BTK M.O.  <BR> <BR>Rader had to be jealous of the media attention that the Hillside Stranglers were receiving. They didn’t need to write poems. They were getting all the notoriety he desired by posing their victims in the weeds. <BR> <BR>Whatever the motivation, Rader was ready in 1979 to target mature women and leave them posed in a field or under a bridge. <BR> <BR>This opens the door to more intense scrutiny of unsolved murders of a similar M.O. that significantly predate the murder of Mrs. Hedge… and for that matter, may predate Anna Williams. <BR> <BR>Lily, <BR> <BR>It’s late and I’m not sure if this makes any more sense than my earlier hypoglycemic ramblings. <BR> <BR>I should get some sleep, rewrite this and find an appropriate thread to post in. <BR> <BR>Mutual &#40;and slightly perverted&#41; admiration coming right back at you, <BR> <BR>LD <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
