</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 12:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lawrence Bittaker  <BR>I hadn&#39;t thought about this case, for years, This was one of the first cases we studied in CJ, I thought by the time we had gotten to this case I had seen everything, I was wrong, This was the only case in my entire 14 year history of studying Serial Killers, that gave me nightmares for a long time. Whoever posted under this name Rader or whoever is one very sick person, and I do not recommend if you are a female that you ever watch the movie made about these two. They were the essence of pure evil.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
