</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 5:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->LOL hahahaha LDawg! Ok, I get it now.  <BR> <BR>Anna - that is why he was so disappointed! He had it all planned and instead had to write an awful script disguised as a poem. It makes the Hedge and Davis crimes much more, ummmm, can&#39;t think of the right word. Not believable, not similar, but somewhere in between. Very nice observation. <BR> <BR>Scooby snacks for your low blood sugar, Lostdog. - Lil<!--/Text--></td></tr>
