<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11245"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 11:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Shag is passed out in the Mystery Mobile… too much reefer again. <BR> <BR>Hey, wasn’t there an episode of Scooby Doo where the monster <BR>turned out to be a dog catcher? <BR> <BR>Hmmmmm… sounds vaguely familiar. <BR> <BR>Lost Doo <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _  <BR> <BR>I have single-handedly unraveled this thread so many times, <BR>I feel a responsibility to review some good observations. <BR> <BR>Two days after Rader’s arrest Topsail asked: <BR> <BR>I find it strange that there are several posters absent now. Some of which were vocal in the last few weeks.  <BR> <BR>Could BTK actually been posting here as a regular poster imposter??? I have a couple of user names in mind but am hesitant to state them. Maybe we should have a roll call with enough allotted time so no one jumps to conclusions. <BR> <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _  _ _ <BR> <BR>On 2/28 Essevi wondered:  <BR> <BR>What does everyone think about this post?  <BR> <BR> <BR>kerri  <BR>Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 2:26 pm:  <BR>  <BR>good point Q- but also keep in mind that &#34;we&#34; meaning ordinary citizens, do not have a God given right to judge mens crimes here on Earth...that was explained to me by my pastor after 9/11 when a lot of people wanted to take the law into theri own hands. This is why we&#40;meaning the U.S.&#41; have the police, FBI, court system etc. that is their job to judge crimes and Gods alone to judge souls. I absolutely agree that Jesus cares about and, yes even loves BTK just as he loves all of His creation. <BR> <BR> <BR>My money says this is THE KR  <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _  <BR> <BR> <BR>Later that day Absinthe was looking for Gramsleuth <BR> <BR>I read nearly everything, but rarely posted, so I&#39;m sure I&#39;m not on anyone&#39;s suspect list, but I&#39;d sure love to see if &#34;Gramsleuth&#34; ever shows up again....that user has some intriguing posts on the Marine Hedge and Delores Davis threads.... <BR> <BR> <BR>To my knowledge Gram is still absent. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>Ed Neil pegged the 12/7 and 12/16 BTK “-“ posts as genuine <BR> <BR>_ __ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ __ _ _  <BR> <BR>On 3/7 Raedelina unearthed a post from “Lawrence Bittaker” <BR> <BR>Note to “Larry”: BTK or not, your choice of user name indicates that you are a friendless, jackassed, chuckleheaded, trip and fall, low SAT scoring LOSER! <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _  <BR> <BR>Johno revisited this charming post from Francis Dolarhyde of “Red Dragon” fame: <BR> <BR>BTK, blah, blah, blah blah… <BR>Your… Avid Fan <BR> <BR>Note to Francis: Congratulations on reading a book!  <BR>Or did your step-mom just let you rent the tape. <BR>Don’t forget to put on your headgear before bedtime. E.S.&amp; D.! <BR> <BR>Lost Dog <BR> <BR>_ __ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>THERE. The thread is good as new! I am 100% guilt-free. <BR> <BR>When looking for possible BTK posts, consider this: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kwch.com/servlet/Satellite?pagename=KWCH%2FMGArticle%2FWCH_BasicArticle&amp;c=MGArticle&amp;cid=1031781463508&amp;path=" target=_top>http://www.kwch.com/servlet/Satellite?pagename=KWC H%2FMGArticle%2FWCH_BasicArticle&amp;c=MGArticle&amp;cid=1 031781463508&amp;path=</a>!news!crime <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/76/698.html?1110520913" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/76/698.htm l?1110520913</a> <BR> <BR>Apparently, Denny the God Catcher disn’t wrote so good. <BR> <BR>DL <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11245-->
<!--Post: 11278--><!--Time: 1110551276-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11278"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hmmm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 6:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve been here... <BR> <BR>Once there were some posts on this board as Hmmm that were not me.  I don&#39;t know if my husband decided to post as me, figuring out my password, or someone else managed to post under my name.  I did write Tom and he had no evidence of another person signing in with my username...I wonder how that happened?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
